-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
20 B% = 3
30 C% = 5
40 D% = 6
50 E% = 0
60 F% = -1
' EQV truth table, on variables so that nothing is folded
70 A% = E% EQV E%
75 PRINT "-1", A%
80 A% = E% EQV F%
85 PRINT "0", A%
90 A% = F% EQV E%
95 PRINT "0", A%
100 A% = F% EQV F%
105 PRINT "-1", A%
' EQV works bit by bit, it is not a boolean operation
110 A% = 3 EQV 5
115 PRINT "-7", A%
120 A% = B% EQV C%
125 PRINT "-7", A%
130 A% = 3 EQV C%
135 PRINT "-7", A%
140 A% = B% EQV 5
145 PRINT "-7", A%
' Priorities: EQV is less priority than AND and OR
150 A% = B% EQV C% AND D%
155 PRINT "-8", A%
160 A% = B% EQV C% OR D%
165 PRINT "-5", A%
' Special cases with a constant operand: reduced by the compiler with a warning
170 A% = 0 EQV B%
175 PRINT "-4", A%
180 A% = B% EQV 0
185 PRINT "-4", A%
190 A% = -1 EQV B%
195 PRINT "3", A%
200 A% = B% EQV -1
205 PRINT "3", A%
----------------------------------------------------------------------
WARNING: at 31:12 line 170 - EQV operation with 0 reduced to inversion; consider to replace EQV with NOT
WARNING: at 33:13 line 180 - EQV operation with 0 reduced to inversion; consider to replace EQV with NOT
WARNING: at 35:13 line 190 - EQV operation with -1 reduced to no operation; consider to remove the useless EQV
WARNING: at 37:13 line 200 - EQV operation with -1 reduced to no operation; consider to remove the useless EQV
